Skip to Main Content2026-2027 General Catalog University of California Santa BarbaraAcademic CalendarSchedule of ClassesPrevious Catalogs Search . . . University of California Santa BarbaraCoursesProgramsDepartmentsAcademics and PoliciesIntroduction to Our CampusAcademicsPoliciesStudent LifeHome/Courses/ENGR 195A - Multidisciplinary Capstone DesignENGR195ADownload as PDFENGR 195A - Multidisciplinary Capstone DesignEngineering SciencesCollege of EngineeringGeneralFull Course TitleMultidisciplinary Capstone DesignAbbreviated Course TitleMULTIDSPLN CAP DESInstructor Name(s)StaffCourse DescriptionThis course allows the coordination of senior students in multiple departments while they undertake a multi-departmental capstone design project. Participating students are required to concurrently enroll in their respective departmental capstone/senior design project courses (ECE 189AB, CMPSC 189AB, ECE 188AB, ME 189ABC), and will additionally enroll in 1 unit of this course for the Fall, Winter and Spring quarters. By taking this course, students will understand practical engineering approaches to collaborate on complex multidisciplinary engineering systems.Units FixedUnits Fixed1Maximum number of times course can be repeated for additional credit0Maximum Units1Advisory Enrollment CommentsMust be enrolled in Capstone project. ProgramsENGR195A is a completion requirement for: BS ME                   - Mechanical Engineering - BSUC Santa BarbaraSanta Barbara, California 93106(805) 893-8000Copyright © 2024 The Regents of the University of California. All Rights Reserved.Terms of Use.  Questions or Comments? Please email us.
